<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Persepolis Fortification Tablets</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persepolis">Persepolis</a> Fortification Tablets are a large archive of clay administrative tablets from the reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-i">Darius I</a>, found at Persepolis. Most are written in Elamite and record the distribution of food and supplies to workers and officials. They show how <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-language">Elamite administrative language</a> and practice were absorbed into the Achaemenid state, a lasting legacy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/persepolis-fortification-tablets.jpg" alt="Persepolis Fortification Tablets" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pentocelo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Persepolis_tablet.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
